# Phenotype-org standard CODEOWNERS (v2 / 2026-06-14)
#
# Source: https://github.com/KooshaPari/phenotype-tooling/blob/main/templates/CODEOWNERS
#
# Place this file at one of:
#     .github/CODEOWNERS        # recommended (GitHub-recognized)
#     CODEOWNERS                # also recognized, repo root
#     docs/CODEOWNERS           # recognized, lower precedence
#
# Rules in CODEOWNERS are "last match wins" — put specific overrides at
# the BOTTOM. The default "*" owner is intentionally set to the
# org-admin handle; override per-path as needed.
#
# Changes from v1 (2026-06-11):
#   + documents the precedence order
#   + adds a worked example block (commented out) for splitting ownership
#     between platform, docs, security, and the catch-all admin
#   + adds a clear "unowned paths = require review" reminder
#   + supports team handles (@org/team) in addition to user handles
#
# When a path has no matching owner, GitHub still requires a CODEOWNER
# approval to merge into a protected branch. Set `require-codeowner`
# in your branch protection to enforce this.

# ── catch-all owner ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every PR must get approval from at least one of these reviewers unless
# a more specific block below overrides.
* @KooshaPari

# ── ownership split (example; uncomment + adapt) ──────────────────────────
# Platform / infra owns CI and deployment surface.
# /.github/        @KooshaPari/phenotype-platform
# /infrastructure/ @KooshaPari/phenotype-platform
# /Cargo.toml      @KooshaPari/phenotype-platform
# /Taskfile.yml    @KooshaPari/phenotype-platform
# /justfile        @KooshaPari/phenotype-platform
# /lefthook.yml    @KooshaPari/phenotype-platform
# /deny.toml       @KooshaPari/phenotype-platform
# /renovate.json5  @KooshaPari/phenotype-platform
# /.editorconfig   @KooshaPari/phenotype-platform
#
# Docs team owns documentation surface.
# /docs/           @KooshaPari/phenotype-docs
# /README.md       @KooshaPari/phenotype-docs
# /CHANGELOG.md    @KooshaPari/phenotype-docs
# /cliff.toml      @KooshaPari/phenotype-docs
# /templates/      @KooshaPari/phenotype-docs
#
# Security team owns secrets, signing, and audit configs.
# /SECURITY.md     @KooshaPari/phenotype-security
# /.github/workflows/reusable-self-merge-gate.yml @KooshaPari/phenotype-security
# /.github/workflows/reusable-policy-gate.yml    @KooshaPari/phenotype-security
# /trufflehog.yml  @KooshaPari/phenotype-security
#
# Rust crates — ownership of individual crates can be set per-crate.
# /crates/quality-gate/    @KooshaPari/phenotype-quality
# /crates/release-cut/     @KooshaPari/phenotype-release
# /crates/fr-coverage/     @KooshaPari/phenotype-fr
# /crates/agent-orchestrator/ @KooshaPari/phenotype-agents

# ── path-based opt-out (example) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment to mark a path as "do-not-require-review"; useful for vendored
# or generated content.
# /vendor/         # no owner
# /node_modules/   # no owner
# /target/         # no owner
# /dist/           # no owner
# /CHANGELOG.md    # auto-generated by git-cliff; no review required
# /Cargo.lock      # auto-generated by cargo; no review required
# /package-lock.json # auto-generated by npm; no review required
# /bun.lock        # auto-generated by bun; no review required
# /pnpm-lock.yaml  # auto-generated by pnpm; no review required
# /yarn.lock       # auto-generated by yarn; no review required
# /poetry.lock     # auto-generated by poetry; no review required
# /uv.lock         # auto-generated by uv; no review required
# /go.sum          # auto-generated by go mod; no review required

# ── notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# To add a team, the team must:
#   1. exist in the org
#   2. have at least one member
#   3. be visible to the repo (Settings → Teams)
# If a team is empty, GitHub silently falls back to the catch-all owner.
#
# To bulk-import a CODEOWNERS file, use the GitHub CLI:
#   gh api -X PUT repos/{owner}/{repo}/codeowners \
#     -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
#     --input CODEOWNERS
